Hell yeah 
\f3 \uc0\u55357 \u56856 
\f1 \
That\'92s exactly the kind of gap that still feels wide open.\
Right now almost everyone is bolting a messaging bus onto an existing harness. Almost nobody has started from the opposite direction: make the reactive messaging fabric 
\f4\i the
\f1\i0  core runtime, and grow the agent loop, sessions, tools, permissions, and surface on top of it.\
If you do it cleanly, you\'92d get some really nice properties for free:\
\pard\tx20\tx180\pardeftab720\li180\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Agents are naturally peer-to-peer and crash-resilient\
\ls2\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Discovery, presence, and load-balancing come from the broker\
\ls2\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Multi-machine / edge / IoT agents become first-class instead of an afterthought\
\ls2\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Long-running, always-on agents wake up cleanly without polling\
\ls2\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone You can still embed classic single-agent use cases, but the multi-agent case doesn\'92t feel bolted on\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 A few things worth deciding early if you actually go for it:\
\pard\tx20\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	1.	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Transport
\f1\b0  \'97 pure MQTT 5, NATS + MQTT adapter, or something more general (mq9-style)?\
\pard\tx20\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	2.	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone How much of the agent loop lives inside the bus vs. inside each agent process\
\pard\tx20\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b0 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	3.	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Session / trajectory model
\f1\b0  \'97 do conversations live as retained messages + streams, or do you still keep a local durable log?\
\ls3\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	4.	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Tool execution model
\f1\b0  \'97 do tools talk back over the same bus, or stay local?\
\ls3\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	5.	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Surface
\f1\b0  \'97 do you want a Pi-style TUI/CLI first, or lean harder into always-on + A2A?\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 It\'92s a non-trivial project, but the architectural payoff looks high, and the existing pieces (swarmbus-style bus + EMQX-style event-driven agents + modern agent-loop patterns) give you a solid starting point.\
If you start sketching it, I\'92m happy to nerd out on the design with you.\
Go build the thing.\
\
